<html xmlns:o="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office" xmlns:w="urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Specification</title></head><body><pre style="font-family:Calibri,sans-serif;font-size:11pt;"># Patient Health Care System — Functional Specification

## Project Overview

Develop a centralized Patient Health Care System to automate patient onboarding and streamline healthcare partner collaboration. This system will automate patient registration, enrollment management, and integration with internal and external healthcare systems. It will also provide secure exchange of patient information, manage data submissions, and ensure compliance through auditability, traceability, and exception handling.

## Scope

**In Scope**
  - Patient registration and enrollment management
  - Patient consent capture, validation, and lifecycle tracking
  - Integration with internal healthcare systems, master data repositories, and external clinical partners
  - Secure exchange of patient and program-related information
  - Processing of both real-time and scheduled data submissions
  - Tracking and monitoring of enrollment and consent status
  - Configurable business rules, routing, and partner-specific processing
  - Auditability, traceability, and regulatory compliance for all transactions
  - Exception handling, error management, and transaction reprocessing
  - Operational dashboards, monitoring, and reporting
  - Rapid onboarding of new partners through configurable workflows and mappings
  **Out of Scope**
  - Custom development outside the defined features
  - On-premises deployment
  - Hardware provisioning and maintenance

## Business Requirements

1. **SHALL**: Support patient registration and enrollment management
    2. **SHALL**: Provide patient consent capture, validation, and lifecycle tracking
    3. **SHALL**: Integrate with internal healthcare systems, master data repositories, and external clinical partners
    4. **SHALL**: Ensure secure exchange of patient and program-related information
    5. **SHOULD**: Support real-time and scheduled data submissions processing
    6. **SHOULD**: Implement tracking and monitoring of enrollment and consent status
    7. **SHALL**: Implement configurable business rules, routing, and partner-specific processing
    8. **SHALL**: Achieve regulatory compliance for all transactions through auditing, traceability, and exception handling

## Functional Requirements

1. Automate patient registration and profile creation
    2. Facilitate patient consent capturing, validation, and tracking
    3. Integrate with internal and external healthcare systems and repositories
    4. Securely exchange patient and program data
    5. Implement real-time and batch data submission processing
    6. Monitor and track enrollment and consent status in real-time
    7. Enable configurable business rules, routing, and partner-specific processing
    8. Ensure auditing, traceability, and regulatory compliance for all transactions
    9. Establish exception handling, error management, and transaction reprocessing mechanisms
    10. Develop operational dashboards, monitoring, and reporting features
    11. Support rapid onboarding of new partners through configurable workflows and mappings
    12. Scale, ensure reliability, and maintain high availability for high-volume healthcare transactions

## Non-Functional Requirements

Performance Requirements
  - **Minimum Response Time**: 0.5 seconds for common operations
  - **Throughput**: Handle 10,000 patient transactions per hour at peak times
  - **Concurrency**: Simultaneously process up to 500 patient transactions

Security Requirements
  - **Authentication**: Use OAuth 2.0 for secure user authentication
  - **Authorization**: Implement role-based access control (RBAC) to manage user permissions
  - **Encryption**: Encrypt sensitive patient data at rest and in transit

Scalability Requirements
  - **Horizontal Scaling**: Dynamically add and remove servers to handle increased load
  - **Database Scalability**: Horizontally scalable, distributed database system

Reliability Requirements
  - **High Availability**: Maintain 99.99% uptime SLA
  - **Backup and Restore Mechanisms**: Automated daily backups with quick disaster recovery

## Success Criteria

1. **Reduction of manual patient enrollment and onboarding processes by 80%**: Measured by comparing pre- and post-implementation processing times and headcount
    2. ** decreased time for patient consent procurement (by X%)**: Measured by comparing the average time taken to capture and validate patient consent pre- and post-implementation
    3. **Improved data accuracy (by Y%)**: Measured by analyzing the discrepancies in patient data before and after system implementation
    4. **Increased healthcare provider satisfaction (% satisfied)**: Conducted through regular post-implementation feedback surveys

## Expected Business Outcome

1. **Decreased operating costs by ($X million over Z years)**: Occupying lower costs due to reduced manual operations and increased efficiency
    2. **Improved patient experience**: Streamlined, digital, and secure patient onboarding and enrollment
    3. **Enhanced partner collaboration**: Reduced errors, expedited data exchange, and quicker onboarding process for healthcare partners
    4. **Improved regulatory compliance**: Ensuring compliance with data privacy and security regulations across multiple geographies
</pre></body></html>